        "id": 13514,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-09-01T02:42:18.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This seems like something that should have an easy answer, but I can’t find it…</p>\n<p>Suppose Tachyon has Unrelenting Momentum in play.</p>\n<p>Action 1: She sprints, gaining a free Nimble Strike.</p>\n<p>Action 2: She sprints again.</p>\n<p>Unrelenting Momentum now grants Tachyon a free sprint. Also, Accelerated Assault grants her a free Nimble Strike. Do I have to choose? Or does she take both actions immediately on gaining them?</p>\n<p>Here’s a variation that really boils down to a second question:</p>\n<p>Action 1: Tachyon sprints, gaining a free Nimble Strike.</p>\n<p>Action 2: She sprints again, this time not taking the free attack, but Unrelenting Momentum grants her a free sprint. She sprints, and this time DOES take the free Nimble Strike. Does Unrelenting Momentum now grant her a free Nimble Strike? In more general terms, does Unrelenting Momentum apply multiple times per turn?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:45:20.857Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 17,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 85.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 13511,
        "topic_slug": "unrelenting-momentum-accelerated-assault",
        "display_username": "Trajector",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": true,
        "user_title": "",
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "This seems like something that should have an easy answer, but I can't find it...\r\n\r\nSuppose Tachyon has Unrelenting Momentum in play.\r\n\r\nAction 1: She sprints, gaining a free Nimble Strike.\r\n\r\nAction 2: She sprints again.\r\n\r\nUnrelenting Momentum now grants Tachyon a free sprint. Also, Accelerated Assault grants her a free Nimble Strike. Do I have to choose? Or does she take both actions immediately on gaining them? \r\n\r\nHere's a variation that really boils down to a second question: \r\n\r\nAction 1: Tachyon sprints, gaining a free Nimble Strike.\r\n\r\nAction 2: She sprints again, this time not taking the free attack, but Unrelenting Momentum grants her a free sprint. She sprints, and this time DOES take the free Nimble Strike. Does Unrelenting Momentum now grant her a free Nimble Strike? In more general terms, does Unrelenting Momentum apply multiple times per turn?",
        "actions_summary": [],
        "moderator": false,
        "admin": false,
        "staff": false,
        "user_id": 11097,
        "hidden": false,
        "trust_level": 2,
        "deleted_at": null,
        "user_deleted": false,
        "edit_reason": null,
        "can_view_edit_history": true,
        "wiki": false,
        "can_accept_answer": false,
        "can_unaccept_answer": false,
        "accepted_answer": false,
        "topic_accepted_answer": false
      },
      {
        "id": 146949,
        "name": "Sonvar",
        "username": "Powerhound_2000",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-09-01T03:26:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>It triggers the first time you use an action for the second time but you have to use it immediately. &nbsp; So you could Sprint - Nimble Strike and then Sprint. &nbsp; At this point you have to use the free sprint or lose it. &nbsp;You can still Nimble Strike again due to Accelerated Assault. &nbsp;Since you didn't use an action directly for Nimble Strike you do not get an extra a Nimble strike from Unrelenting Momentum. &nbsp; Due to the extra sprint that you did you could make four Nimble Strikes due to Accelerated Assault. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:24:57.493Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 13511,
        "topic_slug": "unrelenting-momentum-accelerated-assault",
        "display_username": "Sonvar",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
        "flair_color": "",
        "flair_group_id": 41,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": true,
        "user_title": "",
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>It triggers the first time you use an action for the second time but you have to use it immediately. &nbsp; So you could Sprint - Nimble Strike and then Sprint. &nbsp; At this point you have to use the free sprint or lose it. &nbsp;You can still Nimble Strike again due to Accelerated Assault. &nbsp;Since you didn&#39;t use an action directly for Nimble Strike you do not get an extra a Nimble strike from Unrelenting Momentum. &nbsp; Due to the extra sprint that you did you could make four Nimble Strikes due to Accelerated Assault. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>",
        "actions_summary": [],
        "moderator": false,
        "admin": false,
        "staff": false,
        "user_id": 5464,
        "hidden": false,
        "trust_level": 2,
        "deleted_at": null,
